  "notes": "Paper revisits CMB spectral distortion (COBE/FIRAS) constraints on photon->dark photon conversion, reporting improved 95% c.l. limits on kinetic mixing epsilon vs dark photon mass md (Fig. 8, Fig. 10). Constraint uses |Delta rho/rho| < 6e-5 (FIRAS). Cosmological/CMB bound, not a haloscope, so no local DM density. Data points are APPROXIMATE readings of the FIRAS CosmoTherm exclusion boundary from the log-log figure (axes md=1e-12..1e-3 eV, eps=1e-10..1e-4); precise values not tabulated in text. A separate Neff/CMB+BBN limit gives eps<1.8e-6 for md<~5e-3 eV. PIXIE curves are projections; reported curve here is the observed FIRAS limit. Two illustrative excluded example points quoted in text: (md=1e-7 eV, eps=4e-8) for FIRAS and (md=1e-7 eV, eps=1e-9) for PIXIE. | vector-trace candidate: NR_fraction.pdf colour (0.5, 0.0, 0.5), 120 pts (selected among 11) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 120))",
